From f7a9a7b44e03b3a71d35502534a2a3ea13d5b113 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Lukschander <oliver.lukschander@golf.at>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:46:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: dptx: resend request_display after native DPIN0
 activate

Kernelcache disassembly of AppleDCPDPTXRemotePortProxy (the real
macOS class for a Type-C/dcpext-routed DPTX target -- confirmed
distinct from AppleCIODPTX, which is for direct/fixed ports and uses
an unrelated power mechanism) found that setPowerState's gated
implementation resends request_display (AFK/EPIC method 6, the exact
method dptxport_request_display() already uses) specifically at the
moment the IOKit power domain transitions to active, gated on a
_displayRequested flag -- not merely once, unconditionally, at
initial connect time the way dcp_dptx_connect() currently does it.

Mirror that: once dptxport_native_dpin()'s activate call succeeds
(our closest equivalent signal that this tunneled target's "power
domain" is actually up), resend request_display. Uses only the
existing, already-safe AFK/EPIC method already sent once in every
prior candidate; no new register, address, or APCALL.

See notes/2026-09-23-xnu-power-state-trace.md for the full
kernelcache trace this is based on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dptxep.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dptxep.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dptxep.c
index 147bf5a..cdd5b6a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dptxep.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dptxep.c
@@ -692,9 +692,27 @@ dptxport_call_activate(struct apple_epic_service *service,
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	/* The native USB4 candidate must never configure a physical DP PHY. */
-	if (usb4_native_dpin && dcp_is_usb4_output(dcp))
+	if (usb4_native_dpin && dcp_is_usb4_output(dcp)) {
 		ret = dptxport_native_dpin(service, true, false);
-	else if (dptx->atcphy &&
+		/*
+		 * Real macOS resends request_display (AFK/EPIC method 6,
+		 * same one dcp_dptx_connect() already calls once) from
+		 * inside AppleDCPDPTXRemotePortProxy::setPowerState's gated
+		 * handler, specifically once the IOKit power domain confirms
+		 * active -- not just once, unconditionally, at connect time.
+		 * The native DPIN0/crossbar handshake succeeding here is our
+		 * closest equivalent signal that the "power domain" for this
+		 * tunneled target is actually up, so mirror that resend here.
+		 * See notes/2026-09-23-xnu-power-state-trace.md.
+		 */
+		if (!ret) {
+			int r = dptxport_request_display(service);
+
+			dev_info(dcp->dev,
+				 "USB4: resend request_display after native DPIN0 activate: %d\n",
+				 r);
+		}
+	} else if (dptx->atcphy &&
 	    (!dcp->phy_managed_by_typec || dcp_is_usb4_output(dcp)))
 		phy_set_mode_ext(dptx->atcphy, PHY_MODE_DP, dcp->index);
 
-- 
